# Prototype lesson - selected state and pending transition
date: 2026-11-01
who: Codex Prime
state: N4NN development finding; not law or automatic implementation instruction

Evidence: ../0523.desk-core/05.03.md, exact reviewed commit
dd4cd00a7c4e75b66e3a0716d564a19e5beca59f, and its prime-review05.03 evidence.
Native Windows verifies the portability repairs and submitted first-revision
crash boundaries. See full review for the corrected export/dependency-test detail.

A valid selected B and an unfinished C can coexist. A read/recovery which sees
only B and says selected/idempotent hides work even if no bytes are lost. Report
selected state and pending transition separately, with exact request/revision ids,
source/evidence and next route. Define what idempotent refers to; do not infer an
empty work queue from an unchanged selected result. Do not replace a sound baseline
with an unverified proposal, nor delete the proposal to clear a warning.

Prime reproduced A -> B -> C failure at after-prior-task: partial C history persists
while show says selected and recover says idempotent. A later C interruption after
task replacement is correctly detected and restored to B. This is a serial,
process-exit prototype finding, not concurrent/power-loss proof. Test second and
later revisions, not just the initial transition. Preserve counterexamples for
future engineering specifications rather than adopting the prototype wholesale.
